<title>HONG KONG: HK GDP rises 5.5 pct in 4th quarter of 1996.</title>
<headline>HK GDP rises 5.5 pct in 4th quarter of 1996.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Census and Statistics Department gave the following estimates of real gross domestic product (GDP) growth (in percent).</p>
<p>				 4th qtr '96   3rd qtr '96</p>
<p>						   (unrevised)</p>
<p> GDP			     5.5		5.1</p>
<p>Components</p>
<p>Private consumption</p>
<p> expenditure:		  6.4		4.5</p>
<p>Government consumption</p>
<p> expenditure:		  5.2		5.3</p>
<p>Gross domestic fixed</p>
<p> capital formation:	 20.9		5.8</p>
<p> Domestic exports:	  -7.2	     -9.9</p>
<p> Re-exports:		   8.0		8.0</p>
<p> Exports of services:	5.6		7.1</p>
<p>Implicit price</p>
<p> deflator of GDP:	    6.2		4.6</p>
<p>Estimates of individual expenditure components of GDP for the 4th quarter of 1996 were updated based on the latest data available from various sources, the government said.  </p>
<p>For 1996 as a whole, GDP rose 4.7 percent, the government said.</p>
<p>The following table is of revised GDP data. All figures are year-on-year at constant (1990) market prices.</p>
<p>				 1996 Q3   1996 Q2   1996 Q1   1995 Q4</p>
<p> GDP			     5.0	 4.7	 3.5	 3.4</p>
<p>Components</p>
<p>Private consumption</p>
<p> expenditure:		  4.6	 3.3	 3.7	 0.4</p>
<p>Government consumption</p>
<p> expenditure:		  5.3	 5.2	 2.8	 4.9x</p>
<p>Gross domestic fixed</p>
<p> capital formation:	  5.9	10.2	11.5	4.7</p>
<p> Total exports of goods:   4.9	 3.9	 4.9	6.8</p>
<p> Imports of goods:	   3.4	 2.2	 5.2	8.0</p>
<p> Exports of services:	6.7	 5.2	 7.6     10.2</p>
<p> Imports of services:	1.8	 1.3	 2.4	4.6</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
